#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The unit that gets used to measure altitude, lengths and distances (&eg; km, "
"mi, ft)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "Angle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the notation of angles in coordinates: By default the Degree-"
"Minute-Second notation (&eg; 54°30'00\" ) gets used. As an alternative you "
"can choose decimal degrees (&eg; 54.5°)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Still image"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the map quality that gets displayed while there is no user input. "
"Usually this allows for high map quality as speed is no concern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "During animations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the map quality that gets displayed during map animations (&eg; "
"while dragging the globe). Especially on slow machines it is advisable to "
"set this option to <guilabel>Low Quality</guilabel> as this will give better "
"speed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Place names"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Places often have different names in different languages. The label on the "
"map can show the name in the user's language. Alternatively it can display "
"the name in the official language and glyphs of that place."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Map Font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default font that gets used on the map."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigation Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Navigation configuration dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Navigation configuration dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drag location"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While dragging the mouse there are two standard behaviours when dealing with "
"a virtual globe: The location below mouse pointer will follow the cursor "
"exactly: As a result &eg; the north pole will not stay at the top which can "
"lead to confusion. By default Marble makes sure that north is always up "
"which results in a dragging behaviour where the location below the mouse "
"pointer slightly \"detaches\" from the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "On Startup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default Marble will display the home location immediately after the "
"application has started. As an alternative it can also show the last "
"position that was active when the user left the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "Animate voyage to the target"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When searching for a location Marble can either move instantly to the new "
"location or it can show a travel animation from the previous place to the "
"new place."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
